**Read:** [Petrology — Stephen A. Nelson, Tulane EENS 2120](../sources/Petrology-Nelson-Tulane.lingua#r_1MNEKH4WW2GQRD4FZWNRD1GDPZ), the full metamorphic texture and assemblage notes; [Modeling Metamorphic Rocks Using Equilibrium Thermodynamics — Lanari and Duesterhoeft](../sources/Metamorphic-Modeling-Lanari-Duesterhoeft.lingua#r_08B2X0N88PTC51CSQPZAGWAQV8), the complete equilibrium/domain interpretation review; [Guide to Thin Section Microscopy — Raith, Raase, and Reinhardt](../sources/Guide-to-Thin-Section-Microscopy.lingua#r_2MH30T4MGW8YMVP9SA3Z7XCDSD), the full reaction, inclusion, fabric, and deformation observation sections.

A rock can contain inherited, peak, retrograde, metasomatic, or disequilibrium phases together. A list of every mineral in the section is not automatically an equilibrium assemblage. Identify which domains and textural relationships support coexistence during the event being investigated.

Grain boundaries, inclusions, reaction rims, coronas, foliations, pseudomorphs, zoning, and cross-cutting features constrain different stages. The presence of a phase inside a host can reflect a relative relation but may not establish unchanged peak composition. Several reactions and deformation events can overlap within one specimen.

Choose the chemical/physical domain represented by a phase calculation. An equilibrium approximation can be locally useful even when the entire rock did not equilibrate uniformly. Conversely, selecting a convenient small domain does not justify ignoring component exchange or incompatible textures.

**Work:** describe a complete published or teaching metamorphic section before assigning pressure/temperature. Separate candidate assemblages and stages, explain the evidence for their relationships, and construct an alternative sequence. Identify what additional chemical mapping, structural, or chronological observation could distinguish the accounts.

Read the entire metamorphic texture and equilibrium-domain treatment. The following facies/reaction/calculation work depends on this context; sophisticated minimization cannot compensate for combining minerals that never shared the equilibrium event being inferred.

